# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command chd
shell rust
usage 1   chd ls [<path>...]            the library's disc games under each path (relative to the library), each with its state
usage 2   chd convert <path>... [--fast] [-j <n>] [--output <folder> | --beside]
usage 3                                 convert them to CHD in Compressed (or ChdOutputDirectory, or the folder named),
usage 4                                 or beside each original in the library; each checked three ways and given a package
usage 5   chd check [<path>...]         check converted discs again: chdman's verify, every track, the table of contents
usage 6   chd wait [chd<n>]             follow a chd job that went on in the background (ps lists them, kill stops one)

case the usage, and what a command line refuses
target none
covers 2-4,6
$ chd
out 241
Usage: chd ls [<path>...] | chd convert <path>... [--fast] [-j <threads>] [--output <folder> | --beside] | chd check [<path>...] | chd wait [chd<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library (AppSettings.RomDirectory); / is all of it. See man chd.
status 1
action none
$ chd frobnicate
out 241
Usage: chd ls [<path>...] | chd convert <path>... [--fast] [-j <threads>] [--output <folder> | --beside] | chd check [<path>...] | chd wait [chd<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library (AppSettings.RomDirectory); / is all of it. See man chd.
status 1
action none
$ chd convert
out 303
chd convert: name what to convert, or / for the whole library
Usage: chd ls [<path>...] | chd convert <path>... [--fast] [-j <threads>] [--output <folder> | --beside] | chd check [<path>...] | chd wait [chd<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library (AppSettings.RomDirectory); / is all of it. See man chd.
status 1
action none
$ chd convert psx -j 0
out 283
chd: -j needs a number of threads above 0
Usage: chd ls [<path>...] | chd convert <path>... [--fast] [-j <threads>] [--output <folder> | --beside] | chd check [<path>...] | chd wait [chd<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library (AppSettings.RomDirectory); / is all of it. See man chd.
status 1
action none
$ chd check psx --fast
out 283
chd: --fast is not an option of chd check
Usage: chd ls [<path>...] | chd convert <path>... [--fast] [-j <threads>] [--output <folder> | --beside] | chd check [<path>...] | chd wait [chd<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library (AppSettings.RomDirectory); / is all of it. See man chd.
status 1
action none
$ chd wait
out 25
chd wait: no such chd job
status 1
action none
$ chd wait chd9
out 30
chd wait: no such chd job chd9
status 1
action none
end

case with no library set, every request is refused before anything is read or written
target none
covers 1-5
$ chd ls
out 73
chd: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library to convert.
status 1
action none
$ chd check psx
out 73
chd: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library to convert.
status 1
action none
$ chd convert / --fast -j 2
out 73
chd: AppSettings.RomDirectory is not set: there is no library to convert.
status 1
action none
end
